{#
    Watchdog policy (P1-2 of docs/reviews/code-review-2026-09-15-misra-c99.md)

    A watchdog is only worth arming when exactly one place can prove the system
    is alive.  The component step task is that place: it runs the actual
    control work, so if a sensor read blocks or a component step hangs the
    refresh stops and the MCU resets.

    The refresh used to live in the unrelated "rtc_demo" task, which does no
    real work — it could keep feeding the dog while the control task was hung,
    so the reset never happened.  The watchdog is therefore armed only when a
    designated refresh owner exists; declaring IWDG without one would only
    produce a guaranteed reset loop.
#}
{% set iwdg_refresh_owner = has_components or
       (app_tasks | selectattr('name', 'eq', 'rtc_demo_task') | list | length > 0) %}
{% set iwdg_enabled = has_iwdg and iwdg_refresh_owner %}

